Z||000000||Getaway2k||01-13-2001||09:33 PM||||I just found out last month that my wife and I are going to be parents! Yep, you guessed it, the Fiero has got to go! I'm going to purchase a new S10 extend cab and was wondering how much I might receive for my 86GT (dealer trade-in value)? It's really clean and in excellent condition. It's an auto with air, and the ususal GT features. There are 37,000 original miles on the car. I personally think that I will get burned on a trade-in. I am going to try Ebay prior to trading the car. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||01-13-2001||09:43 PM||||Not sure what trade-in value is. Whatever it is, the dealer will soak you. You might try posting it in the Mall, too. Ya' never know...<BR>Best of luck to you and your family.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 01-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||01-13-2001||09:49 PM||||The dealer will give you the shaft. I can see giving you around $2000 and selling it for $6000 or more. I looked at a 86 GT with 11,500 miles and they wanted $11,000. They gave the guy $4600. DEALERS ARE A RIPOFF!!! Sorry Im done venting....<P>Try eBay... It may sell for more than even you thought.<P><BR>Good Luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Carl<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">        <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!"</B>||||reg||4
Z||000003||Old Lar||01-13-2001||09:58 PM||||go to web site <A HREF="http://www.fiero.net" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.net</A> ||||reg||7
Z||000004||Oreif||01-13-2001||10:00 PM||||With it being winter they will give you less because it is harder for them to sell it. You would get more in spring for it in trade but it will still be a lot less than if you sold it on Ebay, the mall, or even trader online. <P>My advice would be to try and sell it first, You have at least another 8 months before you'll need a bigger car/truck.<P>Congrats on the baby!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cliff D.||01-13-2001||10:09 PM||||I had a dealer offer me $7,500 for my '98 v6 firebird with 68,000 miles just 2 days ago. I wanted to do a double trade-in of that and my wife's '97 ranger for a 2000 ranger 4x4, but ... no deal! Guess I'm stuck with the firebird until it is paid for. Can anyone say 3800 series II fiero?!||||reg||1
Z||000006||skitime||01-13-2001||10:25 PM||||Just my opinion, I had an 87 Gold Gt 20,000 miles with leather seat and all options from 87-89.  My two girls got too big to strap in side by side. My wife told me the get rid of the car because a father shouldn't have a car like that. So I sold the car being the good father. Two years ago I got rid of the wife and wish I got rid of her instead of the car. My feeling is keep the car even if you just store it to keep your expenses down. You will get so little for your Fiero that you will reget for a long time.  Just borrow a little more. Please do it for me.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Getaway2k||01-13-2001||10:43 PM||||Skitime..I know that I'll be singing that same song in years to come if it sells/trades! Bottom line, it's not practical to keep it. I am also in the process of building a new home with a 2 car garage which will house this GT if I can't seal a fair deal. I can use the extra $$$, however, I won't lose my shirt over it. Worse case scenario, it continues to sit in storage until it sells.<P>Thanks for all of the comments everybody!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Phil||01-13-2001||11:04 PM||||They will most likely give you a large trade-in amount but charge you full retail on the truck.||||reg||1
Z||000009||skitime||01-13-2001||11:04 PM||||Where is Kingston Pa? I am near Lancaster, PA.  Keep your car!  Two years from now you will laugh how you considered how you thought you had to sell it. With the low miles you will never find another as good as what you got. Figure out how much you have to borrow without selling the Fiero, I am sure you will still be able to afford the pickup and house.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Motorhead||01-13-2001||11:18 PM||||Cars I kick myself in the butt for selling!!!<BR>1969 Olds 442 convertible,<BR>1970 Roadrunner 383,<BR>1970 'cuda 340<BR>Don't sell the car! Borrow if need be! <BR>Mike ||||reg||1
