Z||000013||Tina||01-14-2001||11:34 AM||||No no no  don't sell.<BR>Kids love fiero's.<BR>Yes, there inpractical at times.<BR>But when push comes to shove, my 3 year old<BR>will run to fiero.<P>Tina||||reg||1
Z||000014||mshill||01-14-2001||12:33 PM||||My wife and I have four kids (5-14 years old) and my wife told me about 18 months ago that it would be nice to have a fun car to go out in instead of taking the minivan or Taurus everywhere.  So, I bought an 86SE... then an 86GT... than an 85SE.  Now I've got 5 cars and two drivers.  Of course, the 86GT is stripped and up on jackstands in the garage being prepped for a rebody, and the 85SE is parked awaiting a V6  (thanks terryk).  But everyother Friday or Saturday night we hop into the 86SE to go out to dinner and a movie.  And yes, the kids would prefer to go in it rather than any other car.  It's like a treat when one of them "gets to go with Dad" somewhere cause they always know dad will be driving the Fiero.<p>[This message has been edited by mshill (edited 01-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||rogergarrison||01-14-2001||02:30 PM||||I deal with dealers everyday. I do lots of body/paint work for some  big dealers. They (not the ones I do work for) generally screw you royal on trades. I just got rid of a Mint restoration 560SL Mercedes Roadster. It had 2 sets of wheels with it, the AMG wheels on it cost almost $4,000. Now, I tried to trade for a new Sebring conv last fall and they offered me $4,000 trade for the car and both wheel sets!!!!!!!, I laughed and left. I sold it to an individual for $18,500 cash instead. So the point is sell it-dont trade.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Cheever2||01-15-2001||09:09 AM||||I knew an accountant for a dealer.  He said: "You will always, always, ALWAYS do better selling it yourself than trading in"!<BR>||||reg||6
